    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0775" n="667" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg667"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Baron Fava</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In answer to your note of this date, and
                    referring to the several personal interviews we have held to-day, I have the
                    honor to inclose a copy of a telegram to the governor of Louisiana, which I have
                    this moment dispatched by order of the President.<anchor n="*" xml:id="d620-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>Trusting that you will see in this telegram the desire and intention of the
                    President to do justice to the Government of Italy,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d620-f1" n="*" xml:id="d620-f1-content">
                <p>For this inclosure see telegram to Governor Nicholls of March 15.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
